## 23. Definition of done

The application is not complete merely because it looks attractive.

The core MVP is complete only when:

1. A parent can register and securely create a child profile.
2. The parent can configure the child's grade, language, and curriculum.
3. The child can complete an assessment.
4. The system records a meaningful, provisional skill profile.
5. The child can open and complete an interactive lesson.
6. Supported answers are graded correctly by tested application logic.
7. Incorrect answers receive constructive feedback.
8. The tutor can provide a suitable explanation or hint through the configured AI service, with a safe fallback when unavailable.
9. The learning planner can select the next activity based on saved learning evidence.
10. Answers, sessions, and progress persist in the database.
11. The parent dashboard shows real saved data.
12. A later session can offer appropriate revision.
13. The app works on mobile and desktop.
14. Protected records cannot be accessed by unauthorized users.
15. Core automated tests pass.
16. The project builds successfully.
17. Setup and deployment documentation is complete.
18. Incomplete integrations and future features are clearly identified.

Demonstrate these workflows with seeded sample data and a test account, without using fabricated production data.

